---
import Container from "../shared/Container.astro";
import Paragraph from "../shared/Paragraph.astro";
import Title from "../shared/Title.astro";
---

<section class="relative py-16 md:py-20" id="philosophy">
    <Container className="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
        <div class="text-center space-y-4">
            <Title>
                Why Harness Engineering Matters
            </Title>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
            <Paragraph>
                Most teams focus on choosing the right LLM. That's the wrong variable. The <strong>harness</strong> — tools, instructions, and context — is what determines outcomes. A well-configured harness turns an average model into an exceptional engineering partner.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Skills are the new unit of engineering excellence. Custom instructions, workflows, and domain knowledge need to be built, tested, versioned, and measured like any other software artifact. Having a skill available doesn't mean it works — activation and outcome testing close that gap.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Real measurement requires real tasks. We evaluate agent performance on challenges derived from actual git history and production codebases — not synthetic benchmarks. Multi-dimensional scoring across architecture, code quality, tests, and team conventions reveals what truly works.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                We're also experimenting with shortening the path from team discussions to design documents with sound architectural decisions, and with organizing knowledge through knowledge graphs (GraphRAG). More on this soon.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
        </div>
    </Container>
</section>
